		{
			"to": "physics/ptolemy",
			"why": "The Harmonics is by the same Claudius Ptolemy of Alexandria who wrote the Almagest, and it applies the same demand to music that his astronomy made of the sky: a numerical model checked against observation, here the ear and the kanon."
		},
		{
			"to": "physics/kepler",
			"why": "Kepler found his third law while writing the Harmonices Mundi of 1619, a book on music and the heavens whose subject, he knew, followed the third book of Ptolemy's Harmonics, and which compares the two in an appendix."
		}
	],
